<title>UK: Achmea Hypo sets 250 million guilder seven-yr bond.</title>
<headline>Achmea Hypo sets 250 million guilder seven-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager ABN AMRO Hoare Govett.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ACHMEA HYPOTHEKENBANK</p>
<p> AMT    250 MLN DFL   COUPON     5.75 PCT  MATURITY    30.DEC.03</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.285   PAY DATE   L06.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875 PCT REOFFER    99.76     SPREAD     *+26 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	*THE LEAD MANAGER CORRECTED THE TERMS ORIGINALLY</p>
<p>		GIVEN, NOT 35 BP OVER BUT 26 BP OVER.</p>
<p>		L-LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    AMST	PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 5-10	SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    =	   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   DOMESTIC</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED APRIL 2003/JAN 2004 DSL -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
